#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md:6
msgid "Tuples"
msgstr ""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md:24
msgid "Like arrays, tuples have a fixed length."
msgstr ""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md:26
msgid "Tuples group together values of different types into a compound type."
msgstr ""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md:28
msgid ""
"Fields of a tuple can be accessed by the period and the index of the value, "
"e.g. `t.0`, `t.1`."
msgstr ""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md:31
msgid ""
"The empty tuple `()` is referred to as the \"unit type\" and signifies "
"absence of a return value, akin to `void` in other languages."
msgstr ""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md:34
msgid ""
"Unlike arrays, tuples cannot be used in a `for` loop. This is because a "
"`for` loop requires all the elements to have the same type, which may not be "
"the case for a tuple."
msgstr ""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md:38
msgid ""
"There is no way to add or remove elements from a tuple. The number of "
"elements and their types are fixed at compile time and cannot be changed at "
"runtime."
msgstr ""
